  "notes": "The producer of the biggest-selling country catalogue in history and the architect of the \"stadium country\" pivot, modelled 1990–1997. His harmony is the entry's most specific claim and it is more chromatic than the Nashville norm: \"the signature verse cell is I – #Idim7 – ii7 – V(add9), with choruses reduced to I–ii–V,\" so the diminished passing chord is authored as `#Idim` — a degree with a dim marker, which the numeral parser reads — and the sevenths live in `extensions`. The single most engine-relevant tracking fact is a negative: on one hit \"both musicians recorded live, with no overdubs and no second take. Model single-take capture with the arrangement decided in the room,\" which is why the fill grid is long and `fillBeforeSection` is off — a single take does not get a punched-in transition. The drums are a fixed band cut live at his own studio, \"2&4 with cross-stick or hats verses and full-kit arena choruses.\" The bass is documented per player: \"live electric bass with root-fifth motion and walking pickups; double bass on the acoustic cuts.\" The melodic habit is the transferable one: \"hooks are improvised by session players and kept — the signature intro arpeggio was invented on the spot by the acoustic guitarist and became the record's identity,\" so the counter is an arpeggio lead rather than a pad. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: high-medium) — \"session personnel, studio and the no-overdub practice are documented; his verbal philosophy is not in reachable sources [LOW-CONF].\" ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the humanize values, the velocity tiers and the counter ratio.",
